      "problem": "Evaluate $\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3,$ we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^3=\\dfrac{4^3}{5^3}\n$$\n\nNow, computing $4^3=64$ and $5^3=125,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4^3}{5^3}= \\dfrac{64}{125} .\n$$",
